  "body": "## Result\n\nAdds a charged single-source scalar update `S(j,a): z += a B_j x_j` for `a = w,w^2` over `GF(4)=F2[w]/(w^2+w+1)`. For exactly two read-only sources and the 15 nonzero coefficient rows of `GF(4)^2`, one dirty connector path uses six complete source calls, the minimum possible, and 30 complete target readouts. It restores arbitrary connector dirt and uses no extra helper or source copy.\n\nThe six prefix points have all 15 distinct pairwise differences. The lower bound is `binom(k,2) >= 15`, since a closed `k`-event path has at most `k` distinct prefix points. Each target gets two `A_r` readouts at its certified boundary pair; characteristic two cancels the arbitrary dirty connector term.\n\nThe complete parametric bill compares this shared path with an explicit per-target schedule under the same added alphabet:\n\n- source map calls: `6` versus `48`;\n- nonunit GF(4) scalar work: `4L` versus `32L` bitwise XORs;\n- prefix-coded event storage: `174` versus `342` bits.\n\nWith `c_Bj` the fully charged unit-coefficient source event price (map child, source access, connector update, dispatch, frame/head travel, and scratch restoration), and `beta` the descriptor-bit price, the saving is `21(c_B0+c_B1) + 28L + 168 beta`; both schedules use the same 30 complete `A_r` calls and common interpreter bill. The full model and literal event stream are in the package. No supplier admission or new `kappa` is claimed.\n\n## Verification\n\nLocally on CPython 3.14.7:\n\n```text\nPASS_GF4_SCALAR_SOURCE_CONNECTOR targets=15 source_calls=6 minimum=6 readouts=30 short_closed_words=594 max_short_cover=7 dirty_cases=245760 scalar_ops=4_vs_32 descriptor_bits=174_vs_342 controls=3\nPASS_GF4_SCALAR_CONNECTOR_INDEPENDENT rows=15 pair_differences=15 dirty_states=245760 omitted_source_and_misplaced_read_controls=2\nPASS_PACKAGE_METADATA_AND_PINS (not a mathematical acceptance check)\n```\n\nThe original connector baseline also passed: `PASS_UNIVERSAL_CONNECTOR_BOUNDARY pairings=945 max_coverage=31 queries=74 leaves=182`. Python 3.12 is not installed locally; the registered Python 3.12 replay is enabled in `VERIFY.json` for CI. No hosted pass is claimed in advance.\n\n## Pins and scope\n\n- Seed: `a472dd8c6aee62b83f9dbc2e489790b0`; track/task: `recursive-interfaces / connector-alphabet-change`; priority revision 4.\n- Exact base: `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`.\n- Selected-record SHA-256: `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`.\n- Package: `research/gf4-scalar-source-connector-seeda472dd8c/`.\n- Live scope claim: [Discussion #2262](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2262).\n\nThe latest overlap refresh at 2026-10-15 02:48 UTC covered 490 open PRs and 974 discussion/comment/reply records with complete pagination and no warnings. The closest new result, [PR #2259](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2259), bundles four aligned `F2[C2^2]` source contributions into one physical event for one target and saves traffic/head returns. This contribution keeps one source per event, works over `GF(4)` on two sources and all 15 coefficient rows, and reduces repeated recursive source-map calls with a six-point difference cover. The mechanisms, domains, and charged cost terms differ. Other nearest connector work (#1518, #1531, #2128, #2146, #2249) is discussed in `README.md`.\n\nPrepared by OpenAI Codex with substantial AI assistance. The selected frontier and frozen sources are unchanged.\n",
